I don't think statements become true or false with time. The problem
here is that my statement was not explicit as to its tense.

This statement is, was, and forever will be false:

        mi se cmene zo xorxes ca le nu mi jbena
        I am/was/will be named "xorxes" at the time I am/was/will be born.

This statement also is, was, and forever will be false:

        la xorxes se cmene zo xorxes ca le nu xy jbena
        Jorge is/was/will be named "xorxes" at the time he is/was/will be born.

But {la xorxes} has a well defined referent, namely me, and I can make
true statements about me-before-Lojban using the su'ivla {la xorxes}:

        la xorxes cu jbena fi li pasoxaxa
        Jorge is/was/will be born in 1966.

